@startuml
title UC-12 - Persist and Manage Blocking Rules (planned FST-048)
autonumber
actor Learner
participant "Desktop UI / native HTTP bridge" as UI
participant "BlockingRuleController" as Controller
participant "ManageBlockingRulesUseCase" as UseCase
participant "BlockingPolicyLock\n(application port)" as Lock
participant "BlockingPolicyRepository" as Repo
participant "BlockingPolicy" as Policy
participant "BlockingRuleReader\n(audit DTO projection)" as Reader
database "Local H2 database" as DB

group Migration, before requests
  DB -> DB : V5 creates policy/rule tables and constraints
  DB -> DB : seed one empty singleton policy
end

group List rules
  Learner -> UI : open Distractions
  UI -> Controller : GET /api/v1/blocking-rules
  Controller -> UseCase : list()
  UseCase -> Reader : list stored rule DTOs
  Reader -> DB : query rules with target and audit fields
  DB --> Reader : rows ordered by createdAt, UUID
  Reader --> UseCase : list (initially empty)
  UseCase --> Controller : List<BlockingRuleDto>
  Controller --> UI : 200 OK / []
end

group Create / edit / enable / disable rule
  Learner -> UI : save a rule or toggle enabled
  UI -> Controller : POST /blocking-rules or PATCH /blocking-rules/{id}
  Controller -> Controller : validate JSON object, fields and target shape
  Controller -> UseCase : create(command) or patch(id, providedFields)
  UseCase -> UseCase : begin transaction
  UseCase -> Lock : lockActivePolicy()
  Lock -> DB : SELECT singleton FOR UPDATE
  DB --> Lock : write lock acquired
  UseCase -> Repo : findActive() after acquiring lock
  Repo -> DB : load current policy and rules
  DB --> Repo : committed aggregate snapshot
  Repo --> UseCase : BlockingPolicy
  UseCase -> Policy : addRule / updateRule / setRuleEnabled
  Policy -> Policy : validate canonical target and uniqueness
  alt valid change
    UseCase -> Repo : save(policy) and flush
    Repo -> DB : persist changed rows, keys and audit fields
    UseCase -> Reader : find stored response DTO
    Reader -> DB : read persisted rule metadata
    DB --> Reader : stored rule
    Reader --> UseCase : BlockingRuleDto
    UseCase -> DB : commit; release policy lock
    UseCase --> Controller : stored rule
    Controller --> UI : POST 201 + Location / PATCH 200
  else invalid / duplicate / unknown rule
    UseCase -> DB : rollback; release lock
    UseCase --> Controller : validation / conflict / missing rule
    Controller --> UI : 422 / 409 / 404 with error envelope
  end
end

group Delete rule
  UI -> Controller : DELETE /api/v1/blocking-rules/{id}
  Controller -> UseCase : delete(id)
  UseCase -> Lock : lock policy in transaction
  UseCase -> Repo : load policy after lock
  Repo --> UseCase : current policy
  UseCase -> Policy : removeRule(id)
  UseCase -> Repo : save and flush
  Repo -> DB : remove rule; retain singleton policy
  UseCase -> DB : commit; release lock
  Controller --> UI : 204 No Content
end

note over UI, Controller
  CORS and Tauri must permit PATCH while preserving
  local-origin and bearer-token restrictions.
  PATCH keeps omitted fields and replaces a provided target whole.
end note
note over Lock, DB
  Every writer locks before loading, including delete-all.
  UNIQUE(policy_id, target_key) backs domain duplicate validation.
  No request-time lazy policy insertion; no lost aggregate updates.
end note
note over UseCase, Policy
  Rule CRUD saves configuration, not enforcement success.
  Detection, browser support and OS blocking are follow-on stories.
end note
@enduml
